  "facts": [
    "The University Heights Bridge, originally the 1895 Harlem Ship Canal Bridge, was relocated in 1908 to span the Harlem River between Inwood and University Heights, preserving its historic swing span.",
    "Designed by William Hubert Burr with ornamental flair from Alfred Pancoast Boller, the bridge’s 264‑foot swing span pivots on a 50‑foot masonry island, a marvel of early 20th‑century engineering.",
    "Between 2000 and 2014, the bridge opened for vessels 114 times, a testament to its continued role in balancing vehicular traffic and maritime navigation on the Harlem River."
